# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enterprise: warp_hypad (Program A) + program_b_em_inverse_design (Program B)
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY TRACKED, and why it looks like generated output but is
# not: results/verification/**. Those are the verification RECORDS -- the
# report, the machine-readable summary, the CSVs a figure is redrawn from. The
# project's policy is that every figure must be reproducible from saved output
# without rerunning the solver, and that a milestone's evidence travels with the
# revision that produced it. They are evidence, not artefacts.
#
# The duplicates of those same records that a build tree writes under
# build/results/** ARE artefacts, and are excluded by the build/ rule below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build trees. build_nooti/ is the OTIlib-disabled configuration.
build/
build-*/
build_*/
cmake-build-*/
out/

# Compiler and linker output, wherever it lands.
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.lib
*.ilk
*.pdb
*.idb
*.exp
*.gcda
*.gcno

# CMake scratch, if a configure is ever run in place.
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
compile_commands.json
Testing/
*.ninja
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log

# Python caches from the plotting scripts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# Configure logs and other transient build chatter.
*_configure.log
compile.log

# Editor and OS noise.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Agent scratch. The session scratchpad lives outside the tree, but a stray
# local copy must never be committed. Deliberately NOT a wildcard on source
# names: an over-broad pattern here would silently drop a real file later.
.claude/
scratchpad/

# Program C: SQLite databases are a pure projection of the committed text
# snapshot, regenerated on demand by tools/snapshot_to_sqlite.py. Committing a
# binary that duplicates a checksummed text file adds no information and can
# drift from it.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal

# Program C: the 50 pc default-volume snapshot is ~60 MB of retrieved Gaia DR3
# records. Regenerate it with tools/import_gaia.py --radius-pc 50; its manifest
# IS committed, so the retrieval is documented and reproducible. The 5 pc and
# 10 pc verification volumes are small and are committed in full.
program_c_astrogation/snapshots/gaia_dr3_50pc.txt
